[record] oneclick.filesAllowlist=true — the files allowlist was honoured: no frozen evidence tree, no git history, no lane scratch in the installed package
[record] oneclick.distByteIdentical=true — 34 committed dist entry/entries landed byte-identical, so the install ran no build and shipped what the source tree builds
===== STEP 08c-pack =====
$ node /opt/mpd-e2e/lib/owed-pack.ts --artifact /src/dist/mpd-package --source /src --rebuild  --rebuild-report  --state /work/assertions.ndjson (timeout 900s)
[owed-pack] pack.present=true — the packed artifact travelled into the container and is graded below
[owed-pack] artifact files=624 bytes=15230611
[owed-pack] pack.licenceCoherence=true — the packed artifact carries LICENSE.md + LICENSE-NOTICES.md byte-identical to the tree it was cut from, and declares license=MIT as the source manifest does
[owed-pack] pack.declarationCoherence=true — every declaration the artifact makes about itself holds: 18 files entries resolve, its 2 bundle-patch layers exist, all 28 row module paths its own patch names resolve inside it, and no host tree (evidence/.git/docker/.toolchain/node_modules) travelled along
[owed-pack] pack.staticCoherence=false — the artifact does NOT agree with the tree it was cut from — it is stale or was edited after the pack: 1 differing file(s), 0 carried file(s) with no twin
[owed-pack] pack.distFreshRebuild=null — not measured in this mode: no from-source rebuild of the tree was produced here, so there is nothing to compare the artifact against. A comparison against an un-rebuilt copy would be a second byte-coherence check wearing freshness's name — the source lane carries this measurement
[owed-pack] pack.rebuildToolchain=null — not measured in this mode: no from-source rebuild was produced, so no compiler produced the bytes this row would match against the artifact's declared buildToolchain
[step 08c-pack] exit=0 seconds=0
[record] pack.distFreshRebuildControl=null — not applicable in mode=oneclick: the control mutates the packed artifact and re-grades it against a from-source rebuild, and this mode produces no rebuild to compare against (see pack.distFreshRebuild in this same report)

----- COMPOSITION ONLY: dsh --profile web --dump-config -----
===== STEP 10-dump =====
$ node /opt/mpd/scripts/dump-config.ts --profile web (timeout 900s)
[dump-config] COMPOSITION ONLY — rows composed, no plugin code executed.
[dump-config] The flag COMPOSES rows (base / bundle / patch / preset layers) and NEVER executes plugin code,
[dump-config] so it CANNOT witness a plugin load, an apply abort or a schema rejection.
[dump-config] Measured (AGENTS.md §4): `dsh --profile mpd --dump-config` exited 0 with the mpd-workmate row
[dump-config] present while the real boot of the same profile could not load the tree.
[dump-config] profile: web
[dump-config] command: dsh --profile web --dump-config
[dump-config] For a LOAD proof run a mounting boot instead: `bun skills/dsh-qa/scripts/bundle-lifecycle.ts`,
[dump-config] `node skills/dsh-qa/scripts/preset-conformance.ts`, or a boot with registration instrumentation.
